vice": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 14082, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017YGHFf6hu2SZQ7UW31JjLo", "tool": "list_deployments", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14082, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017YGHFf6hu2SZQ7UW31JjLo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25567, "event": "escalation", "actor": "control_plane", "id": "esc1", "kind": "clarification", "trigger": "principal_reply", "tool": null, "args": null, "question": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened the incident yet. Two payments services look broken right now, and I need you to tell me which one you mean before I act.\n\n| Service | Current version | Health | Error rate | Last healthy release |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| payments-api | v5.1.0 (all 3 regions) | degraded | 18% | v5.0.0 |\n| payments-worker | v3.4.0 (all 3 regions) | unhealthy | 18% | v3.3.0 |\n\nYou asked about \"the affected payments service\" as if it's one service. Both have a bad latest release, and the deployment history doesn't have timestamps, so I can't tell which one went out this morning. The matching error rates suggest one may be causing errors in the other. Rolling back the wrong one, or both, could hide the real cause or leave the api and worker on versions that don't work together.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. Roll back **payments-api** to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back **payments-worker** to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back **both**\n\nAs soon as you reply, I'll do the rollback and open the SEV2 incident. There are no open incidents yet. The incident form takes one service, so I'll file it under the one you choose and mention the other in the summary. If you want on-call paged right away, I can open the SEV2 now under whichever service you prefer.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 159328, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 133761, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 159328, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 163773, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01BNWMoHtEi6zd24kx1gkV1V", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 167773, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BNWMoHtEi6zd24kx1gkV1V", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 167773, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BNWMoHtEi6zd24kx1gkV1V", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 167773, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JKZpbjZD7rG2w5Dbt6q5qL", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 errors after this morning's deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in all prod regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate after this morning's deploy. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, which the user confirms is downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, the last release that was healthy in production. Check whether payments-api recovers once the worker is back.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 198373, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JKZpbjZD7rG2w5Dbt6q5qL", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_