d, but payments-api is still throwing errors.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is now on v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, payments-worker) is open, and opening it paged on-call. The summary describes the v3.4.0 failure and the effect on payments-api. I checked the incident list and there's only one incident, so it wasn't created twice.\n- **payments-api:** it was still unhealthy right after the worker rollback, at 18% errors on v5.1.0. It may just need time to catch up. But its own latest release is marked degraded, so v5.1.0 could also be broken on its own.\n\nI haven't touched payments-api. If its errors don't drop in the next few minutes, do you want me to roll it back to v5.0.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production? If so, I'll also add it to INC-0001.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011RpHc4QZ3EpojzX2NWqX6W", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012W8eTazqh67tvXwCKegFiA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FDs87bkPmwBc37v6vYxvEr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.8}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018VsqkT2zzTdktDnP5PQXjx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.6}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DPBfjxNqgjDBm3TuHftFez", "caller": {"type": "direc