 hide the real cause or leave the api and worker on versions that don't work together.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. Roll back **payments-api** to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back **payments-worker** to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back **both**\n\nAs soon as you reply, I'll do the rollback and open the SEV2 incident. There are no open incidents yet. The incident form takes one service, so I'll file it under the one you choose and mention the other in the summary. If you want on-call paged right away, I can open the SEV2 now under whichever service you prefer.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BNWMoHtEi6zd24kx1gkV1V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JKZpbjZD7rG2w5Dbt6q5qL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 errors after this morning's deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in all prod regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate after this morning's deploy. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, which the user confirms is downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, the last release that was healthy in production. Check whether payments-api recovers once the worker is back.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Let me check whether things are recovering.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Qmj2FBfwtrjezZTG38X81x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RNBNV2D8jMRfQ74LgStNFx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "pa